      {
        "id": 13039,
        "name": "gphpgl",
        "username": "gphpgl",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/ba9def/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-05-21T07:41:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>When we play, we keep having talks about when certain effects trigger if they are based on \"deal damage\" or \"dealt damage\", so we like to know if we have overlooked a ruling.<br><br>Is a card considered to \"deal damage\", whenever it target a card with damage, no matter the actually effect?<br>Even if that damage is reduced to zero at the source (like \"Damage dealt -1\" on the source)?<br>Even if that damage is reduced to zero from global effects (like \"Damage dealt -1\"/\"Damage taken -1\" from other cards)?<br>Even if that damage is reduced to zero at the target (like \"Damage taken -1\" on the target)?<br>Even if the damage is redirected?<br>Even if the target is immune to the damage?<br><br>Is a card only considered to be \"dealt damage\", when it actually remove hp?<br>Or also when the card is immune the that damage?<br>Or also when the damage is reduced to zero?<br>Or also when the damage is redirected to another card?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:44.248Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 136,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 675.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 13038,
        "topic_slug": "deal-damage-and-dealt-damage",
        "display_username": "gphpgl",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
