        "raw": "<p>A target is considered to deal damage whenever HP is reduced. So anytime the damage is reduced to 0 or the target is immune, they will not deal damage. If the damage is redirected, then they will deal damage to the new target unless it is reduced to 0 or they are immune.</p><p>Like &quot;deal damage&quot;, HP must be removed to trigger any effects on being dealt damage. So immune or reduced to 0 would not have been dealt damage. And in this case, if damage is redirected if the initial target would not have been dealt damage, so none of their effect trigger. However if the new target has a &quot;dealt damage&quot; effect, that would work.</p>",
